<title>CANADA: Canadian Pacific Q4 loss turns to profit.</title>
<headline>Canadian Pacific Q4 loss turns to profit.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996		     1995</p>
<p> Shr   Profit	    C$0.74     Loss	C$2.90</p>
<p> Net   Profit	   257,000     Loss     989,700</p>
<p> Revs		   2,475,000		2,087,500</p>
<p>	   12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr   Profit	    C$2.41     Loss	C$2.41</p>
<p> Net   Profit	   829,100     Loss     823,500</p>
<p> Revs		   8,684,000		7,550,500</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 346,800		  342,000</p>
<p>     (All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Note: Full name is Canadian Pacific Ltd. Unusual item netted out to a gain of C$92.9 million in 1996, largely reflecting the gain of C$120.4 million in the third quarter relating to the repayment of perpetual 4 percent consoldiated debenture stock. In 1995, unusual items netted out to losses of C$774 million in the fourth quarter and C$739.5 million for the full year, consisting primarily of the restructuring charge at Canadian Pacific Railway of C$704 million in the fourth quarter.</p>
<p>((Reuters Montreal bureau 514-985-2434))</p>
</text>
